<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ayrarat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ayrarat was a central province of historic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, in the plain of the Aras river around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Mount Ararat</a>. It contained many of the kingdom's capitals, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxata">Artashat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vagharshapat">Vagharshapat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a>, and in the Bagratid period also Ani in its district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shirak">Shirak</a>. Its lands now lie mostly in Armenia and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ayrarat.jpg" alt="Ayrarat" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Event.Horizon.000 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayrarat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
